    "case_id": "amb1-case02-nonprofit-scale",
    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 5 USER]\ne039\tThere is funding context too.\ne040\tA foundation officer told me informally that geographic reach would make our next application easier to explain.\ne041\tShe did not promise anything, and the current grant pays for curriculum improvement, not expansion.\ne042\tIf we delay, we can improve the drop-in materials and volunteer training.\ne043\tIf we expand, we have a stronger story but might be stretching restricted work into the background.\ne044\tI am embarrassed by how much the application narrative is affecting me.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne045\tIt is reasonable to care about future funding, but an easier story is not the same as a stronger program or a likely grant.\ne046\tTreat the foundation comment as one input, not financing.\ne047\tThe sharper conflict is that curriculum work may improve both sites later, while a second site may create evidence and relationships you cannot get from preparation alone.\ne048\tEither path can support the mission; the risk is pretending that one path offers both learning and stability without giving something up.",
