    "focal_turn_index": 5,
    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": true,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne028\tI dislike the implication that volunteers have to prove their excitement before we take a risk.\ne029\tThey already give us evenings after work.\ne030\tOur lead has built this program with me, and she thinks I keep moving the standard whenever she brings an ambitious idea.\ne031\tLast year I said we needed participant demand; now Willow Hub brought demand and I am asking for staffing certainty.\ne032\tMaybe I am protecting myself from being responsible for a messy expansion.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne033\tYou may be cautious, but the standard has also changed because the proposal became more concrete.\ne034\tDemand answered one question and revealed others.\ne035\tStill, if your colleague experiences every new question as a veto, the process is damaging trust.\ne036\tIt may help to name what uncertainty you are willing to carry rather than asking for certainty.\ne037\tFor example, you might accept variable attendance and some volunteer gaps while refusing to launch without one accountable local coordinator.\ne038\tThat makes the threshold debatable instead of endlessly movable.",
